# Baked in at `npm run build` — set in the hosting “Environment” for the build step.
# Vite is configured to read these from the shell *and* .env; Hostinger’s panel sets process.env
# and `vite.config.ts` injects them (fixes empty import.meta.env in the client).
# Either name works (Hostinger often uses VITE_API_BASE_URL):
# VITE_API_URL=https://api.yourdomain.com
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://backend.yourdomain.com
# Local dev: leave unset or:
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:4000
#
# Alternative without rebuild: in index.html add a script *before* the main bundle:
#   <script>window.__SNOW_BITES_API_URL__="https://api.yourdomain.com";</script>
